#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:193
msgid "Optimize Offscreen Rendering"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:194
msgid ""
"When enabled, Containers that are below the fold are only rendered when the "
"visitor scrolls near them. This reduces the amount of work the browser does "
"during the initial load, which can make pages load faster and scroll more "
"smoothly — especially on content-heavy pages. Headers, footers, and the "
"first (few) above-the-fold Containers are automatically exempted so hero "
"content is unaffected. You can override the behaviour per Container in its "
"Extras tab."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:199
msgid "Above The Fold Container Count"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:200
msgid ""
"Number of Containers at the top of the page body that are treated as "
"above-the-fold and therefore kept out of the offscreen-rendering "
"optimization. Increase this if your pages typically start with more than "
"one hero-style Container. Lower it to 0 for page types that start straight "
"into content with no hero. Individual Containers can still override this "
"default."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:213
msgid "Emojis Script"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:214
msgid ""
"If you don't use emojis you can improve performance by removing WordPress' "
"emojis script."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:217
#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:227
#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:305
#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:327
msgid "Enable"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:218
#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:228
#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:306
#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:328
msgid "Disable"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:223
msgid "jQuery Migrate Script"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:224
msgid ""
"If you are not using any deprecated jQuery code, you can disable this "
"script to improve performance."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:233
msgid "Load jQuery On Every Page"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:234
msgid ""
"Avada loads jQuery only on pages where a script needs it. Set to 'on' to "
"load it on every page, for custom code ( Code Fields, Code Blocks, child "
"theme scripts ) or a plugin that uses jQuery without asking for it."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:239
msgid "Load jQuery In Footer"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:240
msgid ""
"Set to 'on' to defer loading of jQuery to the footer of the page. This will "
"only take effect if no other jQuery dependent scripts are added to the "
"head. Turning this on can cause JS scripts to break, use with caution."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:245
msgid "Load Stylesheets In Footer"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:246
msgid ""
"Set to 'on' to defer loading of the stylesheets to the footer of the page. "
"This improves page load time by making the styles non-render-blocking. "
"Depending on the connection speed, a flash of unstyled content (FOUC) might "
"occur."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:252
msgid ""
"<strong>IMPORTANT NOTE:</strong> .htaccess doesn't exist or it is not "
"writable."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:257
msgid "Enable Compression & Browser Caching"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:258
msgid ""
"Set to 'on' to add compression and browser caching rules to the .htaccess "
"file. Brotli is used when the server offers it, with Gzip as the fallback. "
"<strong>IMPORTANT:</strong> This option works only on Apache and LiteSpeed "
"web servers, and needs mod_deflate (or mod_brotli) and mod_expires enabled."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:263
msgid "Enable Video Facade"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:264
msgid ""
"Use video facade in order to load video player only when video is played. "
"<strong>IMPORTANT:</strong> This option is only applied to YouTube and "
"Vimeo elements."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:273
msgid "Clear Object Cache "
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:274
msgid ""
"Set to 'on' to clear WP's object cache on post edit, post deletion, and "
"Avada Form Entries page view. This is useful, if your setup or hoster uses "
"persistent object caching, to make sure that queries update when you add or "
"remove posts."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:279
msgid "Persist Query Cache"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:280
msgid ""
"Set to 'on' to store Avada's internal query results in the persistent "
"object cache, instead of only for the duration of each page request. This "
"only has an effect, if your setup or hoster uses persistent object caching. "
"<strong>NOTE:</strong> Some object cache plugins log a notice for these "
"entries."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:285
msgid "Number Of Post Revisions"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:286
msgid ""
"Controls how many revisions WordPress keeps for each post or page. Set to "
"\"-1\" to use the WordPress default (unlimited), \"0\" to disable revisions "
"completely, or any higher number to keep only that many of the most recent "
"revisions. Limiting revisions keeps the database smaller and prevents the "
"post editor from running out of memory on content-heavy pages that have "
"built up a large revision history."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:301
msgid "SVG Media Upload"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:302
msgid ""
"Enable upload of SVG files and improve performance through their smaller "
"image and logo file size. SVG files can carry scripts, so administrators "
"can always upload them, while other roles need SVG Uploads switched on "
"under Permissions. Form upload fields only accept SVG files when they list "
".svg explicitly and the form was created by a user who may post unfiltered "
"HTML."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:311
msgid "Upload Image Format"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:313
#. translators: "System Status" page link.
msgid ""
"Select a modern format to use when uploading new images to the media "
"library. If you choose AVIF but your server is not able to convert to this "
"format, it will automatically fall back to webP. You can also convert all "
"your existing images on the %s page."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:317
msgid "WebP"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:318
msgid "AVIF"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:323
msgid "Keep Original Upload Images"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:324
msgid ""
"If enabled, not only the image with its original upload format will be "
"kept, but also the created thumbnails. This will increase the filesystem "
"storage use of your images."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:336
msgid "Display Image Format"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:337
msgid ""
"If set to \"original\", Avada will try to load the images in their original "
"upload format. If set to \"modern\", it will try to load the images in the "
"upload image format you set above."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:340
msgid "Modern"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:341
msgid "Original"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:350
msgid "WordPress Image Quality"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:352
#. translators: "Regenerate Thumbnails" plugin link.
msgid ""
"Controls the quality of the generated image sizes for every uploaded image. "
"Ranges between 0 and 100 percent. Higher values lead to better image "
"quality but also higher file sizes. <strong>NOTE:</strong> After changing "
"this value, please install and run the %s plugin once."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:352
#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:364
#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:378
msgid "Regenerate Thumbnails"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:362
msgid "WordPress webP Image Quality"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:364
#. translators: "Regenerate Thumbnails" plugin link.
msgid ""
"Controls the quality of the generated image sizes for every uploaded webP "
"image. Ranges between 0 and 100 percent. Higher values lead to better image "
"quality but also higher file sizes. <strong>NOTE:</strong> After changing "
"this value, please install and run the %s plugin once."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:377
msgid "Avada Image Sizes"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:378
msgid ""
"Choose which Avada image sizes should be created for every image uploaded "
"to the Media Library. <strong>NOTE:</strong> Image sizes used in legacy "
"areas/features of Avada are marked with (L). When you remove image sizes "
"here, please check your site to make sure all layouts display correctly. "
"After changing this value, please install and run the %s plugin once."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:381
msgid "200px Width"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:382
