msgid ""
"Visitor Analytics is turned off under Marketing → Experiments & Links. The "
"Visitor Tracking Mode below currently only applies to operational features "
"such as abandoned cart recovery."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/privacy.php:767
msgid ""
"The site-wide ceiling on how visitors may be identified by tracking "
"features. \"No Identifiers\" issues no cookies or hashes of any kind, not "
"even for operational features. \"Anonymous\" counts visitors without "
"cookies — they are never recognised on a return visit, no consent banner is "
"required, and A/B testing and statistics still work day-scoped. \"Session "
"Cookies\" allows capped tracking cookies, \"Full\" additionally allows a "
"persistent visitor identifier — both subject to visitor consent when the "
"Privacy Consent Tools are enabled. Storage visitors explicitly ask for "
"(wishlists, comparisons) is not governed by this setting."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/privacy.php:779
msgid ""
"Allow joining a visitor's browsing history to their contact record when "
"they log in, check out or click a campaign email link. This is the switch "
"that turns anonymous statistics into personal data — with it off, contacts "
"are still created for emails and orders, but their browsing history is "
"never attached to them."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/privacy.php:787
msgid "Email Engagement Tracking"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/privacy.php:788
msgid ""
